# IT 140 Module Four Assignment
# Higher/Lower Game Pseudocode Template
#
# Complete the TODO prompts below with your own pseudocode.
# Keep this file in .pseudo format for submission.
#
# Use clear indentation to show decisions and repeated behavior.
# Your finished pseudocode should address every requirement in the
# current Module Four Assignment Guidelines and Rubric.

START hilow_game

    # Establish a valid guessing range.
    Input the lower bound
    Input the upper bound
    WHILE the lower bound is greater than or equal to the upper bound
        Output "The lower bound must be less than the upper bound."
        Input the lower bound.
        Input the upper bound.
    END WHILE

    # Establish the number the player is trying to guess.
    Generate a random number between the lower bound and upper bound
    Store the random number as the target number.

    # Play the game.
    Obtain a guess from the player.
    WHILE the guess is less than the lower bound OR the guess is greater than the upper bound
        Output "The guess must be between the lower and upper bounds."
        Obtain another guess from the player.
    END WHILE

    WHILE the guess is not equal to the target number
        IF the guess is less than the target number
            Output "Nope, too low. Guess another number:"
        ELSE
            Output "Nope, too high. Guess another number:"
        END IF
        Obtain another guess from the player.
        WHILE the guess is less than the lower bound OR the guess is greater than the upper bound
            Output "The guess must be between the lower and upper bounds."
            Obtain another guess from the player.
        END WHILE
    END WHILE

    Output "You got it!"

END hilow_game

